From: Takoserver Native source candidate
Subject: [SOURCE ONLY v6.12] refuse owned single-verdict edits before CT and skb mutation

Against v6.12 with the retained tako_terminal base and NFQUEUE admission piece.
Uses the actual dequeued entry and existing predicate/cleanup only.
Config-off/unowned behavior stays unchanged. No terminal/grant or build claim.

diff --git a/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c b/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c
--- a/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c
@@ -1435,6 +1435,12 @@
 	entry = find_dequeue_entry(queue, ntohl(vhdr->id));
 	if (entry == NULL)
 		return -ENOENT;
+
+	/* Refuse this real entry before CT or packet edits from the verdict. */
+	if (unlikely(tako_terminal_block(entry->state.net, entry->state.pf))) {
+		nfqnl_reinject(entry, NF_DROP);
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	/* rcu lock already held from nfnl->call_rcu. */
 	nfnl_ct = rcu_dereference(nfnl_ct_hook);
